{
  "program": "CBACT04C",
  "caseId": "case10",
  "description": "The '23' window and the 'DEFAULT' retry, both lines and both reads. The account row is acctdata.txt row 0 VERBATIM, so ACCT-GROUP-ID is ten spaces and the key :210-212 builds misses every group in the file. DISCGRP holds two rows verbatim - A000000000 type 01 category 0001 and DEFAULT type 01 category 0001, both at fifteen percent - which is what makes the miss meaningful: a matching category exists under another group, and the program still does not see it, because the group id is part of the sixteen-byte DIS-GROUP-KEY. So :418 and :419 display, :437 moves 'DEFAULT' into the key, and the retry at :444 succeeds. Note what the '23' window leaves behind: READ ... INTO transfers on success only, so between the two reads DIS-GROUP-RECORD still holds whatever it held before - which is why the retry at :444 has no INVALID KEY phrase and why a SECOND '23' is fatal rather than merely quiet. 1000.00 at fifteen percent is 12.50.",
